    "quoted": [
      "photo targets, photo gates, glint bands, achro ceilings, spread limit \u2014 plan round-10 audit",
      "structure gates (plate 8, broad plate 12, speckle 2, fringe +4, seg z 5, jag p90 0.10, clip 2) \u2014 plan Task 23",
      "structure weights 25/25/15/15/10/10 and composite R = 0.40P + 0.30S + 0.15C + 0.15V \u2014 plan round-10 audit",
      "colour checks r(sat,L) <= -0.5, achro <= 2.5 %, mean sat >= 110 \u2014 plan Task 25"
    ],
    "reconstructed": [
      "S verdict scale (pass 1 / half 0.5 / fail 0): the audit published S = 4.3 but not its arithmetic; these weights with 0/0.5/1 verdicts give sapphire 42.5/100 -> 4.25 -> 4.3, and R then reproduces 3.7 exactly. Fringe is the only detector that can score half: its gate is read as the two-sided band [-4, +4], so sapphire -20.9 (no additive fringe, desaturated rim) = half and citrine +12.0 (additive) = fail.",
      "coherence floor 0.60: the audit reports coherence as a pass at 0.744/0.746 without stating the floor; any floor in 0.25..0.74 gives the same verdict for both stones.",
      "S is the sapphire stone (the gate stone) in the composite; citrine S is reported alongside. Mean-of-stones S = 3.875 would give R 3.6, which does not reproduce the frozen 3.7.",
      "photo gate count 74 = 72 cell gates + 2 exposure-spread gates; the published 45 is the cell-gate count (the audit table sums to 45/72). Both denominators are printed by audit.py."
    ],
    "not_from_pixels": [
      "V (vision) 3/10 sapphire, 4/10 citrine is the round-10 owner/vision read; audit.py echoes it from this file and never measures it."
    ]
  },
